      "id": 1,
      "text": "Sale Creek’s name comes from a historic coal mine that operated from 1868 until 1913.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.chattanoogan.com/2025/8/27/507716/The-Creeker-Magazine-Featuring-History.aspx",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s mail trains ran from 1880 to 1967, delivering letters via steam locomotives before diesel RPO cars took over.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.chattanoogan.com/2025/8/27/507716/The-Creeker-Magazine-Featuring-History.aspx",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1992, Curtis Coulter produced a historical calendar that listed every notable event that ever happened in Sale Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.einpresswire.com/article/535444840/an-excursion-to-the-past-a-historical-journey-of-sale-creek-and-coulterville-tn",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Coulter also authored a 2021 book, *An Excursion to the Past*, detailing Sale Creek’s history from 1775 to today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
